#: src/postulo/core/server_forms.py
msgid "Yes: a person may have a picture of the whole page kept, sent by their browser extension or drawn here from the kept source with scripts and the network off. A picture taken in somebody's browser shows the page as they were seeing it, signed in or not. No, or not set: nobody's captures keep one."
msgstr "Jo: eng Persoun kann e Bild vun der ganzer Säit behale loossen, geschéckt vun hirer Browser-Erweiderung oder hei aus dem behalene Quelltext gezeechent, mat Skripten an Netzwierk ausgeschalt. E Bild, dat am Browser vun iergendengem gemaach gouf, weist d'Säit esou, wéi déi Persoun se gesinn huet, ugemellt oder net. Nee oder net gesat: kenger seng Erfaassunge behalen eent."

#: src/postulo/core/server_forms.py
msgid "Yes: a person may have the page's source kept beside what was read from it, exactly as it was parsed, so that a capture can be checked against it and read again by a better parser. It is kept as text and never shown as a page. No, or not set: nobody's captures keep it, whatever they have chosen."
msgstr "Jo: eng Persoun kann de Quelltext vun der Säit nieft deem behale loossen, wat dorauser gelies gouf, genee esou wéi en analyséiert gouf, sou datt eng Erfaassung domat verglach an duerch e bessere Parser nach eng Kéier gelies ka ginn. En gëtt als Text behalen an ni als Säit gewisen. Nee oder net gesat: kenger seng Erfaassunge behalen en, egal wat se gewielt hunn."

#: src/postulo/core/server_forms.py
msgid "Yes: anyone who finds the address may create an account. No: invitation only. An empty instance always offers the sign-up form, so somebody can become the first account."
msgstr "Jo: jiddereen, deen d'Adress fënnt, kann e Kont uleeën. Nee: nëmme mat Invitatioun. Eng eidel Instanz bitt ëmmer de Registréierungsformulaire un, sou datt een den éischte Kont uleeë kann."

#: src/postulo/core/server_forms.py
msgid "Yes: somebody who arrives through the identity provider is signed straight in, without being asked for a code as well. Say yes only if you know that provider checks identity at least as carefully as Postulo would. It never applies to a password sign-in, and it removes nobody's authenticator app. A passkey already counts on its own and needs no setting."
msgstr "Jo: wien iwwer den Identitéitsubidder kënnt, gëtt direkt ugemellt, ouni datt zousätzlech no engem Code gefrot gëtt. Sot nëmmen dann jo, wann Dir wësst, datt deen Ubidder d'Identitéit op mannst esou suergfälteg kontrolléiert, wéi de Postulo et géif maachen. Fir eng Umeldung mat engem Passwuert gëllt et ni, an et hëlt kengem seng Authentifikatiouns-App ewech. En Zougangsschlëssel zielt souwisou fir sech eleng a brauch keng Astellung."

#: src/postulo/core/server_forms.py
msgid "Yes: somebody who has forgotten their password can ask for a code at their primary address and type it back. A code rather than a link, because mail scanners follow links and would spend one before the person read it. It is never a second factor: an authenticator app is still asked for. Offered only while this instance's mail is actually getting through."
msgstr "Jo: wien säi Passwuert vergiess huet, kann e Code op seng Haaptadress ufroen an en aginn. E Code a kee Link, well Mail-Scanner Linken opmaachen an en esou verbrauche géifen, ier d'Persoun en gelies huet. Et ass ni en zweete Faktor: no der Authentifikatiouns-App gëtt weider gefrot. Gëtt nëmmen ugebueden, soulaang d'E-Maile vun dëser Instanz wierklech ukommen."

